{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/init()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0VACycfc","symbolKind":"init","title":"init()","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Initializer","remoteSource":{"fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L33"}},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init()"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The matrix with no vertices and no columns."}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/init()":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The matrix with no vertices and no columns."}],"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/init()","type":"topic","title":"init()","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init()"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"IncidenceMatrixModule"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of column "},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"kind":"symbol"}}}